00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:16,440
Damn it!

270
00:18:16,620 --> 00:18:18,480
Those bastards got ahead of us!

271
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:20,340
We gotta catch up! Hurry!

272
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:23,132
No pirate worth his salt would miss this!

273
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:27,760
Without further ado, let the games begin!

274
00:18:28,320 --> 00:18:29,150
Die!

275
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:40,360
Look at that!

276
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:42,031
Over there, on the coast!

277
00:18:44,340 --> 00:18:46,869
The Navy's got the
whole island surrounded!

278
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,280
It's an entire fleet!

279
00:18:49,260 --> 00:18:50,140
You see?

280
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:53,137
They've made sure no one
can escape from this place!

281
00:18:53,220 --> 00:18:56,357
And if we can't get out and tell
the world what they've done here,

282
00:18:56,440 --> 00:18:59,146
then they can erase their
crimes from history!

283
00:18:59,540 --> 00:19:03,697
They're planning to kill the locals and
steal the island's natural resources!

284
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:06,757
And three weeks from
today when their little

285
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:09,757
murder game is over every
last one of the hundred

286
00:19:09,840 --> 00:19:14,517
thousand rabbits will be
dead don't you understand

287
00:19:14,600 --> 00:19:18,520
before we even realized
it we've gone to hell

288
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:26,977
Yeah but we just got to survive
three weeks if we can pull

289
00:19:27,060 --> 00:19:31,897
that off we'll be free they're
never going to let you go they've

290
00:19:31,980 --> 00:19:35,617
done this before there are no
survivors from any game wait

291
00:19:35,700 --> 00:19:38,637
what if they're just gonna kill
us all why would they give us

292
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:42,817
hope Because if you have hope
you'll run for your lives they

293
00:19:42,900 --> 00:19:45,737
don't want to kill people who
know that they'll die that's no

294
00:19:45,820 --> 00:19:50,617
fun for them you can't survive
playing by their rules this

295
00:19:50,700 --> 00:19:54,520
sick game is rigged against us
so we have to turn it on its head

296
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:06,630
St.

297
00:20:06,713 --> 00:20:09,340
Garling has earned a
whopping 100,000 points!

298
00:20:09,560 --> 00:20:11,972
He must be aiming for high-score rabbits!

299
00:20:17,540 --> 00:20:18,900
Yes, it's off!

300
00:20:19,820 --> 00:20:21,160
Nice jaws, pal.

301
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:23,106
Good to have a sharkfish man.

302
00:20:23,280 --> 00:20:24,460
Uh, thank you.

303
00:20:24,740 --> 00:20:26,858
Not used to feel comfortable anyway.

304
00:20:27,080 --> 00:20:28,540
This doesn't make sense.

305
00:20:29,040 --> 00:20:30,397
They got the information.

306
00:20:30,480 --> 00:20:31,597
I made sure of that.

307
00:20:31,680 --> 00:20:37,560
But neither the pirates nor the Navy have
done a thing why not I don't understand.

308
00:20:37,880 --> 00:20:38,998
What are you doing?

309
00:20:39,940 --> 00:20:41,380
What I do best?

310
00:20:41,960 --> 00:20:42,937
Manipulating intel!

311
00:20:43,020 --> 00:20:45,357
There's just one ticket out of here!

312
00:20:45,440 --> 00:20:46,957
the prizes for the game!

313
00:20:47,040 --> 00:20:48,060
the prizes?

314
00:20:49,160 --> 00:20:52,180
One is a Devil Fruit
with mythical strength.

315
00:20:52,620 --> 00:20:57,057
It lets you transform into an azure
dragon They've got another one to a

316
00:20:57,140 --> 00:21:01,597
Devil Fruit that gives you the power to
send people flying to faraway islands

317
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:03,386
It's called the pawpaw fruit.

318
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:06,717
If we can eat one of those
fruits, we'll have it made.

319
00:21:06,800 --> 00:21:11,457
We'll track them down, soar over the
blockade, and leave this hellhole in the dust.

320
00:21:11,540 --> 00:21:12,893
There's no way, though.

321
00:21:13,060 --> 00:21:15,077
The prizes are at the
center of the island.

322
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:18,160
Soon as they spot us,
we're done for. Don't fret.

323
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:20,600
I'm a thief and a pro at wiretapping.

324
00:21:21,080 --> 00:21:25,080
Two weeks ago, I leaked some intel
about this island to the outside.

325
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:28,117
That means pirates will be
flooding this place soon.

326
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:29,677
They'll want that sweet treasure.

327
00:21:29,760 --> 00:21:31,289
It's gonna be pandemonium!

328
00:21:32,620 --> 00:21:36,100
Thing is, that alone won't be
enough to pull off our plan.

329
00:21:36,460 --> 00:21:38,677
One of us will have to serve as a decoy.

330
00:21:38,760 --> 00:21:41,819
We gotta distract the
Celestial Dragons to rob them.

331
00:21:42,480 --> 00:21:43,600
A decoy?

332
00:21:46,380 --> 00:21:47,280
I'll do it.

333
00:21:48,600 --> 00:21:49,430
Kuma!

334
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:53,461
I'm big and tough, so I think I
can survive longer than the others.

335
00:21:53,700 --> 00:21:57,280
Besides, I don't want
to see anyone else hide.

336
00:21:59,000 --> 00:21:59,920
Yee-haw!

337
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:01,350
Ah!

338
00:22:01,433 --> 00:22:03,940
Now we're talking Kuma, and
I won't let you die either.

339
00:22:04,320 --> 00:22:06,420
Let's escape God Valley, together!

340
00:22:14,740 --> 00:22:16,300
Oh! What the hell?

341
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:20,706
They're coming from the east!

342
00:22:21,660 --> 00:22:23,620
It's the Rocks Pirates!

343
00:22:23,900 --> 00:22:26,200
The Rocks Pirates? But why?

344
00:22:26,860 --> 00:22:28,497
Wait, there are others too!

345
00:22:28,580 --> 00:22:31,120
It's a whole swarm of infamous pirates.

346
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:32,740
There was no alert.

347
00:22:32,980 --> 00:22:33,917
How could this happen?

348
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:34,880
Fire, now!

349
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:42,900
Don't bother, you Navy dogs.

350
00:22:44,540 --> 00:22:46,820
Rocks Pirates, follow me!

351
00:22:49,380 --> 00:22:51,000
What was that, Rocks?

352
00:22:51,160 --> 00:22:54,000
You think you can order
me around? Go to hell!

353
00:22:54,560 --> 00:22:56,080
Oh, stop it, Newgate.

354
00:22:56,420 --> 00:22:57,660
Don't do this now.

355
00:22:59,260 --> 00:23:01,554
Planning to do something today, Stussy?

356
00:23:01,700 --> 00:23:03,620
You're one to talk, Gloriosa.

357
00:23:04,080 --> 00:23:06,020
It's finders' keep, as I say.

358
00:23:06,500 --> 00:23:07,600
We good with that?

359
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:12,300
You won't get a thing.

360
00:23:12,680 --> 00:23:14,700
I'll be taking both fruits.

361
00:23:15,660 --> 00:23:18,131
Come on, Lin-Man, you can't even use them.

362
00:23:19,200 --> 00:23:21,060
They're my treasure, mate.

363
00:23:23,620 --> 00:23:25,180
Rox is a damn fool.

364
00:23:25,340 --> 00:23:26,737
He'll forget why we're even here.

365
00:23:26,820 --> 00:23:28,517
Let's run in and check the treasure.

366
00:23:28,600 --> 00:23:31,657
Stop talking like you are
a leader, you hypocrite!

367
00:23:31,740 --> 00:23:33,937
I'm about to wreck this whole island.

368
00:23:34,020 --> 00:23:37,097
Get your head out of the clouds
and quit trying to act tough.

369
00:23:37,180 --> 00:23:39,297
Let's grab the treasure
and take to the sea.

370
00:23:39,380 --> 00:23:41,477
I heard that Roger
might be showing up too.

371
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:42,897
I'll take him on.

372
00:23:42,980 --> 00:23:44,745
What did I just say, you brat?

373
00:23:44,920 --> 00:23:46,497
This fight will decide it all.

374
00:23:46,580 --> 00:23:48,957
That's what we want, all of us.

375
00:23:49,040 --> 00:23:50,880
Then let's settle this.

376
00:23:54,580 --> 00:23:56,997
The rocks pirates have made landfall.

377
00:23:57,080 --> 00:23:58,297
Pirates here!

378
00:23:58,380 --> 00:23:59,817
What are you defense doing?

379
00:23:59,900 --> 00:24:02,377
If anything happens to
us, we'll see you dead.

380
00:24:02,460 --> 00:24:04,097
Reporting in!

381
00:24:04,180 --> 00:24:06,317
Dangerous pirates are
coming from all directions.

382
00:24:06,400 --> 00:24:08,017
We can't stop them.

383
00:24:08,100 --> 00:24:09,257
How did they know?

384
00:24:09,340 --> 00:24:11,437
This event was strictly confidential.

385
00:24:11,520 --> 00:24:13,637
Their current objective is unclear.

386
00:24:13,720 --> 00:24:14,757
Incoming!

387
00:24:14,840 --> 00:24:15,997
On the western shore.

388
00:24:16,080 --> 00:24:18,100
That's the Roger pirates.

389
00:24:24,240 --> 00:24:29,097
In a whole year, you have any idea
how much I've been stewing on this?

390
00:24:29,180 --> 00:24:30,857
Gonna be a wild one.

391
00:24:30,940 --> 00:24:33,317
Roger, no calling first dibs!

392
00:24:33,400 --> 00:24:34,437
Just because you're the captain.

393
00:24:34,520 --> 00:24:36,880
Yeah, let's go.

394
00:24:38,400 --> 00:24:39,937
Pull back the marines.

395
00:24:40,020 --> 00:24:41,697
Protect the celestial dragons.

396
00:24:41,780 --> 00:24:42,837
So pathetic!

397
00:24:42,920 --> 00:24:44,997
What was the point of the blockade?

398
00:24:45,080 --> 00:24:46,877
Holy nights to battle!

399
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:47,820
All right.

400
00:24:50,100 --> 00:24:51,677
Roger and rocks.

401
00:24:51,760 --> 00:24:53,637
I don't think we should

402
00:24:53,720 --> 00:24:54,797
hold out A

403
00:24:54,880 --> 00:25:01,880
piece

404
00:25:04,260 --> 00:25:05,090
of Roger

405
00:25:11,860 --> 00:25:13,700
Is this a Devil Fruit?

406
00:25:14,360 --> 00:25:15,190
Yeah.

407
00:25:15,273 --> 00:25:16,897
Got no idea which is which, though.

408
00:25:16,980 --> 00:25:17,810
Just eat.

409
00:25:22,700 --> 00:25:23,900
There you are.

410
00:25:24,080 --> 00:25:25,280
That was close, huh?

411
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:27,073
Eva, are you all right?

412
00:25:29,240 --> 00:25:31,140
Now for my other treasure.

413
00:25:33,060 --> 00:25:34,460
Quick, eat it!

414
00:25:39,500 --> 00:25:42,265
You better fork that over
now, you little shit.

415
00:25:42,420 --> 00:25:43,479
Don't think twice.

416
00:25:48,720 --> 00:25:51,800
Eat that fruit and survive, Kuma!

417
00:25:56,060 --> 00:25:57,880
Only one of us has to live!

418
00:26:01,900 --> 00:26:04,800
A single survivor means we win!

419
00:26:08,040 --> 00:26:09,320
You did it!

420
00:26:09,520 --> 00:26:10,900
Run, Kuma, run!

421
00:26:18,800 --> 00:26:21,700
Listen to me, buccaneer boy.

422
00:26:23,040 --> 00:26:26,357
You will live as a
slave, then you will die.

423
00:26:26,440 --> 00:26:28,680
That is your lot in life.

424
00:26:29,020 --> 00:26:32,480
Your fate has been decided
by the course of history.

425
00:26:34,540 --> 00:26:36,200
He's someone important.

426
00:26:37,800 --> 00:26:40,237
He says some people are born to rule.

427
00:26:40,320 --> 00:26:41,597
That's not right.

428
00:26:41,680 --> 00:26:44,437
Some people are born to be slaves.

429
00:26:44,520 --> 00:26:46,520
Why are we born at all?

430
00:26:48,020 --> 00:26:49,437
I don't know much.

431
00:26:49,520 --> 00:26:54,497
But if I really do have some
power, Then I want to be like Mock.

432
00:26:54,580 --> 00:26:57,437
I want to protect people from suffering.

433
00:26:57,520 --> 00:27:00,337
I want to free as many slaves as I can.

434
00:27:00,420 --> 00:27:01,957
This is why.

435
00:27:02,040 --> 00:27:04,500
Your people need to be eliminated!

436
00:27:07,600 --> 00:27:09,357
Get back here, rocks.

437
00:27:09,440 --> 00:27:11,300
Out of my way, Roger!

438
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:15,840
This incident would fade into
the dark shadows of history.

439
00:27:17,720 --> 00:27:19,760
They wrote about Garp's heroics,

440
00:27:19,900 --> 00:27:22,397
but didn't mention anything
else that happened that day.

441
00:27:22,480 --> 00:27:25,280
The people in power
write our history for us.

442
00:27:25,660 --> 00:27:28,248
This reporter Morgans
is nothing but a hack!

443
00:27:28,380 --> 00:27:31,400
We were there, and we might
never learn the truth.

444
00:27:31,720 --> 00:27:34,020
All we can do is hope and pray.

445
00:27:34,640 --> 00:27:37,697
How long are you going to
keep doing that, by the way?

446
00:27:37,780 --> 00:27:38,760
I'm praying.

447
00:27:39,460 --> 00:27:42,107
For all the lives that
I wasn't able to save.

448
00:27:42,420 --> 00:27:43,660
Would you cut it out?

449
00:27:43,940 --> 00:27:45,600
You did pretty damn good.

450
00:27:45,840 --> 00:27:48,860
Even in all that chaos,
you saved 500 people.

451
00:27:49,040 --> 00:27:50,158
He's right, Kumaji.

452
00:27:50,340 --> 00:27:51,380
You were awesome.

453
00:27:51,740 --> 00:27:53,957
They were all so grateful that they cried.

454
00:27:54,040 --> 00:27:55,380
And that I cried too.

455
00:27:57,220 --> 00:28:00,160
But I never forget.

456
00:28:00,460 --> 00:28:02,460
Those hands can do more than pray.

457
00:28:02,620 --> 00:28:04,502
They're the hands of liberation.

458
00:28:05,280 --> 00:28:06,110
Liberation?

459
00:28:06,420 --> 00:28:07,250
Really?

460
00:28:08,720 --> 00:28:10,280
You just have to survive.

461
00:28:10,580 --> 00:28:11,410
Don't give up.

462
00:28:11,493 --> 00:28:13,840
The warrior of liberation will save you.

463
00:28:18,320 --> 00:28:21,057
So your family ran a church
when you were born, huh?

464
00:28:21,140 --> 00:28:24,258
Well, that would explain
why you turned out this way.

465
00:28:28,860 --> 00:28:29,690
Ha!

466
00:28:29,773 --> 00:28:30,603
So long, pals!

467
00:28:30,700 --> 00:28:32,053
I'm heading out to sea!

468
00:28:32,140 --> 00:28:34,397
I'm free now, so I gotta enjoy it!

469
00:28:34,480 --> 00:28:35,860
I hope we meet again.

470
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:37,647
I'll never forget your face.

471
00:28:39,160 --> 00:28:40,984
Actually, I get that one a lot.

472
00:28:41,360 --> 00:28:43,860
Big bro, I still gotta figure out my life.

473
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:45,277
I'll stay with Kumachi.

474
00:28:45,360 --> 00:28:46,190
Good luck.

475
00:28:47,840 --> 00:28:50,380
Farewell, my darling compatriots.

476
00:28:55,920 --> 00:28:56,750
All right.

477
00:28:57,520 --> 00:28:59,457
I'm the eldest here by four years.

478
00:28:59,540 --> 00:29:02,011
So that means it's my job to keep you fed.

479
00:29:07,600 --> 00:29:09,520
You can do it, kumachi!

480
00:29:12,280 --> 00:29:13,380
Looking good!

481
00:29:13,680 --> 00:29:14,621
Let's sell them!

482
00:29:15,560 --> 00:29:17,100
No more scavenging.

483
00:29:17,340 --> 00:29:18,240
No stealing.

484
00:29:18,660 --> 00:29:20,980
We'll work for our food, honest-like.

485
00:29:22,040 --> 00:29:24,500
Now let's head off to market. Yeah!

486
00:29:27,640 --> 00:29:29,240
We sold it all!

487
00:29:29,680 --> 00:29:31,340
I worked up an appetite.

488
00:29:31,840 --> 00:29:33,157
What do you want to eat today?

489
00:29:33,240 --> 00:29:36,200
I'll be fine with anything.
You can pick. Yay!

490
00:29:37,300 --> 00:29:38,130
Dadan?

491
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:41,540
Never seen you two around.

492
00:29:41,680 --> 00:29:42,510
Who are you?

493
00:29:42,593 --> 00:29:43,423
Who are you?

494
00:29:43,506 --> 00:29:44,540
You sure are huge.

495
00:29:44,840 --> 00:29:45,800
How old are you?

496
00:29:46,060 --> 00:29:47,354
I'm big, but I'm nine.

497
00:29:47,660 --> 00:29:49,680
You're joking! No way!

498
00:29:53,400 --> 00:29:54,660
You're a liar!

499
00:29:55,840 --> 00:29:56,960
Big monster!

500
00:30:07,440 --> 00:30:10,660
I'm sorry, we got off to a bad start.

501
00:30:10,840 --> 00:30:12,134
Jimmy is usually nice.

502
00:30:16,220 --> 00:30:17,050
What?

503
00:30:17,880 --> 00:30:19,020
The bump's gone.

504
00:30:19,260 --> 00:30:21,900
It doesn't hurt anymore. It's magic!

505
00:30:22,340 --> 00:30:23,869
That was so cool, Kumachi!

506
00:30:24,160 --> 00:30:25,140
You're awesome!

507
00:30:28,780 --> 00:30:29,610
Kumanshee!

508
00:30:29,693 --> 00:30:30,680
Kumanshee! Kumanshee!

509
00:30:33,980 --> 00:30:35,140
Alright, let's eat.

510
00:30:35,300 --> 00:30:36,476
Don't gotta tell me!

511
00:30:42,120 --> 00:30:44,900
I want more! Here. Are you sure?

512
00:30:49,640 --> 00:30:50,640
So yummy!

513
00:30:51,640 --> 00:30:55,117
It's okay if you want to eat a
lot, but we'll have to work hard.

514
00:30:55,200 --> 00:30:56,030
Okay!

515
00:31:00,040 --> 00:31:03,120
By the way, what age
did you become a slave?

516
00:31:05,260 --> 00:31:06,460
When I was four.

517
00:31:06,780 --> 00:31:07,640
Same as me!

518
00:31:08,060 --> 00:31:11,177
Don't know if that's something
for you to smile about.

519
00:31:11,260 --> 00:31:12,320
I'm four.

520
00:31:14,720 --> 00:31:17,380
I'm four. Hmm? Ginny?

521
00:31:20,360 --> 00:31:21,880
Come on, Ginny!

522
00:31:53,580 --> 00:31:56,460
It was so bright.

523
00:31:56,960 --> 00:31:58,100
It's coming here!

524
00:32:19,540 --> 00:32:22,120
I'm so happy.

525
00:32:26,960 --> 00:32:27,817
I have wanted to.

526
00:32:27,900 --> 00:32:33,017
I don't even know

527
00:32:33,100 --> 00:32:37,360
what it meant.

528
00:32:37,640 --> 00:32:39,540
I don't want anyone else.

529
00:32:43,380 --> 00:32:44,877
I don't wanna be able...

530
00:32:44,960 --> 00:32:47,580
I'm not leaving.

531
00:32:47,720 --> 00:32:49,200
It won't be me anymore.

532
00:32:50,320 --> 00:32:55,257
I got your hands on my hand.

533
00:32:55,340 --> 00:33:01,077
I can't eat the sky,

534
00:33:01,160 --> 00:33:05,560
but the deep sea will light up.

535
00:33:07,400 --> 00:33:12,760
We are every day, we are not every day.

536
00:33:12,920 --> 00:33:15,460
We are not here, we are here.

537
00:33:45,460 --> 00:33:47,277
